-- title:
--   owner0 mode1 compatibility boundary mass rows
-- statement:
--   For owner 0 and mode 1, let $N_{s,w}$ be the stated integer boundary-table entry, $D=10^{12}$, $\alpha_s$ the cell weight, and $c_{s,a}$ the multiplicity of atom $a$. Every cell $s$ and four-letter word $w$ satisfy
--
--   $$\frac{N_{s,w}}{D^5}=\mathbf{1}_{\operatorname{shape}(s)_{2}=0}\frac{\alpha_s}{D^5}\sum_{a:\,a_{1}=w}c_{s,a}.$$
--
--   Thus the boundary rows encode exactly the boundary contribution to the released compatibility potential.
-- source:
--   Exact released rational CW profile and joint atom counts.

